# OPTIONAL: Pre-fill the Spotify Client ID via env var (skips the in-app wizard).
#
# Lyripop's normal flow is the in-app first-run wizard, which walks you through
# creating a personal Spotify Developer app and pastes the Client ID into
# %APPDATA%\com.m6bernha.lyripop\ — most users don't need this file.
#
# This env var is here for development workflows where you want the app to
# come up pre-configured without clicking through the wizard each rebuild.
#
# Get a Client ID by:
#   1. Go to https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard
#   2. Create app (any name). Tick "Web API". Save.
#      Set redirect URI: http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback
#   3. Copy the 32-char Client ID below
#
# Resolution order at runtime: env var > stored (wizard) > source default.
VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
